    "slug": "hallucination-proofing",
    "title": "AI Hallucinations: How to Make ChatGPT and Claude Stop Inventing Facts",
    "description": "In September 2026, a California lawyer was fined $999.99 after filing court documents containing seven case citations that didn't exist — invented by an AI tool she trusted. Days earlier, New Mexico's highest court fined another attorney $5,000 after ChatGPT fabricated entire witness testimony in a murder appeal. These are professionals who lost real money because they treated AI output as verifie",
